        "bio": "<p><span>Nurse Practitioner Whitney Gibbs has been practicing since 2016, with a focus in family medicine. Her areas of clinical interest include infectious disease, primary care and urgent care. She is board-certified by the American Association of Nurse Practitioners and certified in Department of Transportation. </span></p>\n<p><span>Whitney received her Bachelor of Nursing at Texas Woman's University in Denton, her Master of Science through University of Houston at Sugar Land, TX, and Walden University. She is a member of the Sigma Theta Tau International Honor Society of Nursing, and is a member the American Association of Nurse Practitioners. </span></p>\n<p><span>On a personal note, Whitney is a dog lover who enjoys travel, history and spending time with her family.</span></p>",
