        "bio": "<p>As a board-certified Family Nurse Practitioner, Tamica Green (Gr-ee-n) enjoys using her range of skills and experience to help patients achieve and maintain good health. Originally from northeast Louisiana, Tamica relocated to the Houston area approximately four years before joining Village Medical.</p>\n<p>Tamica earned her Bachelor of Science in Nursing from the University of Louisiana at Monroe in 2005. She worked in Labor and Delivery within the high-risk unit of a state hospital in Louisiana for eight years before returning to school to earn her Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) from Grambling State University in 2013. Tamica also worked with patients in urgent care and family practice for six years. In addition to family practice, Tamica has clinical interests in women's health and preventative medicine. She is a member of the Houston Area Nurse Practitioners (HANP) Association.</p>\n<p>When Tamica is not working, she enjoys spending time with family, traveling, going to the movies and reading Christian fiction novels. She also has a passion for the arts.</p>",
