        "bio": "<p>Natasha Harrison, MD, CHCQM, has been practicing since 2009. She specializes in Internal Medicine, with clinical interests in the management of chronic diseases such as hypertension and type 2 diabetes, mind-body and lifestyle medicine.</p>\n<p>Dr. Harrison received her Bachelor of Science degree in Biology from the University of North Texas in Denton, TX. She then attended medical school at the University of Texas Medical Branch in Galveston, TX. She completed her residency in Internal Medicine at Allegheny General Hospital in Pittsburgh, PA, and fellowship in Geriatric Medicine at Southwestern Medical Center in Dallas, TX. She is certified by the American Board of Internal Medicine in Internal Medicine and Geriatric Medicine and also holds a certification in Health Quality Care and Management.</p>\n<p>Dr. Harrison is a member of the American College of Physicians and the American Board of Quality Assurance and Utilization Review Physicians. She is dedicated to providing high-quality care to her patients, focusing on their individual needs and health goals.</p>\n<p>When not at work, Dr. Harrison enjoys indoor and outdoor gardening. She loves to travel and learn about different cultures.</p>",
