        "bio": "<p>Khaula Raza, AGNP-C, has been caring for patients since 2017. Her main focus is on adult and gerontology primary care. She has a deep interest in chronic and acute conditions and clinical research.</p>\n<p>Khaula earned her Associate Degree in Nursing from Houston Community College. She then completed her Bachelor of Science in Nursing at the University of Texas at Arlington. She also has a Master of Science in Nursing from the University of Texas Medical Branch at Galveston. She is currently working towards a Post Masters Pediatric Primary Care Nurse Practitioner degree at UT Arlington, with an expected graduation date in Fall 2025. Khaula is also a proud member of the American Association of Nurse Practitioners (AANP), Gerontological Advanced Practice Nurses Association (GAPNA), and Texas Nurse Practitioners (TNP).</p>\n<p>In her personal life, Khaula is passionate about making a difference for the better. She is a big proponent of patient and family education, and believes that \"learning is a never-ending process\". When she's not working or studying, Khaula enjoys sewing and drawing.</p>\n<p>Khaula is married and has two beautiful daughters, both of whom are also in healthcare related fields. She enjoys spending time with her family and friends. Khaula is fluent in Urdu and Hindi, in addition to English.</p>",
