        "bio": "<p><span style=\"font-family: Georgia, Palatino, Times, 'Times New Roman', serif;\">Dr. Madhavi Reddy <em>(Re-dee)</em> attended both medical school and residency training at Baylor College of Medicine, where she had the honor of serving as Chief Resident. Dr. Reddy is a board-certified physician with over 20 years of experience in Family Medicine. Recently, she was recognized as a Fellow of the American Academy of Family Physicians.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: Georgia, Palatino, Times, 'Times New Roman', serif;\">Dr. Reddy has clinical interests in preventative medicine, women’s health and clinical research. Her career path has been full of rich experiences, beginning with many years as a small-town physician. Dr. Reddy has also worked as a physician for a cutting-edge pharmaceutical research company, putting new medicines on the market.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: Georgia, Palatino, Times, 'Times New Roman', serif;\">Dr. Reddy comes from a family of physicians and enjoys being a mother to three lovely children. In her spare time, she takes pleasure in experiencing the world through culture, art, music and philosophy. She understands the importance of family and community and is looking forward to serving yours.</span></p>",
