        "bio": "<p>Yana Romanov, PA-C <em>(Rah-mah-nav)</em>, was born in Baku, Azerbaijan and moved to NYC when she was 12. She went on to graduate from Touro College PA School and then received her master’s degree in Health Management and Finance at New York University. She worked at an internal medicine practice for four years and then moved to Massachusetts. She continued to work at a family practice for nine years. She then moved to Houston in September 2015 and joined Village Family Practice.</p>\n<p>She has been a PA for 20 years and her special interests include preventative medicine, women’s health and chronic conditions.</p>\n<p>Yana is married and has two kids. In her free time she enjoys traveling, reading, shopping and spending time with her family.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
