        "bio": "<p><span>Dr. Faiza Wajid began practicing in 2014 with a focus on family medicine and clinical interest in geriatrics, women’s well exams, preventative care, diabetes, hypertension and cardiovascular disease. She is board-certified by the American Osteopathic Board of Family Physicians. </span></p>\n<p><span>Dr. Wajid received her Bachelor of Science in Molecular Biology at Benedictine University in Lisle, IL, attended medical school for her Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine at Midwestern University-Chicago College of Osteopathic Medicine in Downers Grove, IL, and completed her residency at Western Michigan University School of Medicine in Kalamazoo, MI, and a traditional internship at the University of Medicine and Dentistry of New Jersey, Stratford, NJ. </span></p>\n<p><span>She is a member of the American Academy of Family Practice, American College of Osteopathic Family Physicians, Medical Society of Vermont, Medical Society of NH, American Osteopathic Association and Midwestern University Alumni Association.</span></p>\n<p><span> In addition to English, Dr. Wajid speaks fluent Urdu and Hindi. </span></p>\n<p><span>On a personal note, she likes to read, paint, cook and travel to new places to learn about various cultures. She enjoys being active in nature and spending time with her children.</span></p>",
